Hi Nick,

In your second call:

fNM.NR.PATH  <- sem(NM.NR.PATH ,data=D_, se="robust.sem", estimator = 'MLM', bootstrap=2000)

as far as I understand,  se="robust.sem" asks lavaan to compute robust SE, not bootstrap SE. Therefore, bootstrap=2000 is ignored.

You should see the following in the printout:

Parameter Estimates:

  Standard errors                           Robust.sem
  Information                                 Expected
  Information saturated (h1) model          Structured

The SE row is Robust.sem, not bootstrap.

Hope this helps.

-- Shu Fai

